 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by a regex in `tracker/validation.py` that did not enforce a top-level domain (TLD) in email validation. The fix updated the `EMAIL_RE` regex to require a dot and domain suffix (e.g., `@example.com`), ensuring invalid emails like 'carol@localhost' are rejected with a 422 error.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/validation.py b/tracker/validation.py\nindex 7df7cdf..0828bb8 100644\n--- a/tracker/validation.py\n+++ b/tracker/validation.py\n@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ PRIORITY_MAX = 5\n TAG_MAX_LENGTH = 30\n MAX_TAGS = 10\n USERNAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^[a-z0-9_]{3,32}$\")\n-EMAIL_RE = re.compile(r\"^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+$\")\n+EMAIL_RE = re.compile(r\"^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$\")\n PASSWORD_MIN = 8\n \n TASK_FIELDS = {\"title\", \"description\", \"priority\", \"assignee_id\", \"due_at\", \"tags\", \"status\"}\n",
